[11.850493, "o", "PASS SP-B2: steer was submitted during the slow tool; the model first got it in request 2, after 1 tool result(s)\r\nPASS SP-B3: killed during a tool; the new process made 3 model request(s); the forgotten text was in 0 of them\r\nPASS SP-B5: killed during the slow tool of turn 1; the new process resumed from the last copy and ended \"done\". The slow tool ran 2 time(s) (attempts 1, 2) with call id tool:1795006148080:2j51ku7tb58, tool:1795006148416:8uz57x3i6yv; model calls in the new process: 3\r\nPASS SP-B5 (turn 2): killed during the lookup of turn 2, after the copy of turn 1. slow: attempt 1 tool:1795006149268:l9wvsxz31d. lookup: attempt 1 tool:1795006149723:82mfl8u8exu, attempt 2 tool:1795006150059:q27uz45109. Model calls in the new process: 2\r\nPASS SP-B6: killed after the copy before the action; the call id before the kill and after the resume: tool:1795006150499:jspqvd3j1x and tool:1795006150499:jspqvd3j1x; actions done: 1. The id comes from the tool call in the model answer, which the journal stores\r\nPASS SP-B6 (30 turns): a task of 30 tool calls has 30 different call ids\r\nPASS SP-B7 (3 turns): 3 copies; the last copy is 118784 bytes; the mean time to make and send one copy is 14.5 ms\r\nPASS SP-B7 (30 turns): 30 copies; the last copy is 167936 bytes; the mean time to make and send one copy is 16.4 ms\r\nPASS SP-B9: the copies of task A are gone; task B ended \"done\"\r\nPASS SP-B10 (safe): killed after the endpoint answered; distinct action ids sent: 1; the answer of the model: \"done\"; model requests in the new process: 1\r\nPASS SP-B10 (unsafe): killed after the endpoint answered; distinct action ids sent: 2; the answer of the model: \"done\"; model requests in the new process: 2\r\n"]
[11.855988, "o", "PASS SP-B11: killed before the next copy; the new process submitted both messages again with the same request ids; the last model request has the first message 1 time(s) and the second 1 time(s)\r\n"]
